CM Half-wave dipole in free space, swept through resonance.
CM
CM A 0.5 m long wire of radius 1 mm, 21 segments, driven at the centre
CM segment by a 1 V source, swept from 265 to 305 MHz in 2 MHz steps.
CM
CM This is the textbook case: a thin resonant dipole is a little shorter
CM than half a wavelength, and its feedpoint resistance at resonance is
CM around 70 ohms. check-nec2c.py finds where the reactance crosses zero
CM and checks both numbers, which exercises the whole NEC2 core - geometry
CM parsing, the interaction matrix, the LU solve and the field integrals -
CM against a result that does not come from nec2c itself.
CE
GW 1 21 0.0 0.0 -0.25 0.0 0.0 0.25 0.001
GE 0
EX 0 1 11 0 1.0 0.0
FR 0 21 0 0 265.0 2.0
XQ
EN
